    <description>
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Cross-ATA Interface and Discipline BREX</title>
        <para>
          This BREX defines rules for cross-ATA chapter references and interface 
          constraints for ATA 31 (Indicating/Recording) AMM data modules. It ensures 
          proper separation of responsibilities and prevents redefinition of content 
          owned by other ATA chapters.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>ATA 24 - Electrical Power Interface</title>
        <para>
          ATA 31 indicating/recording systems depend on ATA 24 for electrical power.
        </para>
        <para>
          PERMITTED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Reference to ATA 24 power supply specifications
        </para>
        <para>
          - Circuit breaker identification and location
        </para>
        <para>
          - Power consumption specifications for ATA 31 equipment
        </para>
        <para>
          - References to ATA 24 procedures for power system verification
        </para>
        <para>
          PROHIBITED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Electrical power generation system descriptions
        </para>
        <para>
          - Battery system maintenance procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          - Bus tie logic and load shedding procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          - Generator or inverter maintenance
        </para>
        <para>
          REFERENCE FORMAT: Use "Refer to AMM 24-xx-xx" for power system procedures
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>ATA 42 - Integrated Modular Avionics Interface</title>
        <para>
          ATA 31 display and recording systems often interface with ATA 42 IMA platforms.
        </para>
        <para>
          PERMITTED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Data bus connection specifications (ARINC 429, AFDX, etc.)
        </para>
        <para>
          - Signal interface requirements for ATA 31 equipment
        </para>
        <para>
          - Software load part numbers for display applications
        </para>
        <para>
          - References to ATA 42 data loading procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          PROHIBITED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Core IMA module descriptions and maintenance
        </para>
        <para>
          - Network configuration procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          - Operating system updates or modifications
        </para>
        <para>
          - Partition management procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          REFERENCE FORMAT: Use "Refer to AMM 42-xx-xx" for IMA platform procedures
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>ATA 45 - Maintenance Systems Interface</title>
        <para>
          ATA 31 recording systems interact with ATA 45 central maintenance systems.
        </para>
        <para>
          PERMITTED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - References to data download interfaces
        </para>
        <para>
          - FDR/CVR/QAR data retrieval procedures specific to ATA 31 equipment
        </para>
        <para>
          - BITE (Built-In Test Equipment) access for ATA 31 systems
        </para>
        <para>
          - Fault code interpretation for ATA 31 faults
        </para>
        <para>
          PROHIBITED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Central maintenance computer (CMC) hardware maintenance
        </para>
        <para>
          - Overall system health monitoring architecture
        </para>
        <para>
          - Cross-system fault correlation procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          - Maintenance data upload/configuration management
        </para>
        <para>
          REFERENCE FORMAT: Use "Refer to AMM 45-xx-xx" for CMC procedures
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>ATA 23 - Communications Interface</title>
        <para>
          ATA 31 displays may show communications data from ATA 23 systems.
        </para>
        <para>
          PERMITTED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Display symbology for communications status
        </para>
        <para>
          - References to communications data sources
        </para>
        <para>
          - Display configuration for communication page layouts
        </para>
        <para>
          PROHIBITED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Radio equipment maintenance procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          - Communication system functionality descriptions
        </para>
        <para>
          - Antenna system maintenance
        </para>
        <para>
          - SATCOM or HF radio troubleshooting
        </para>
        <para>
          REFERENCE FORMAT: Use "Refer to AMM 23-xx-xx" for communications procedures
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>ATA 22 - Auto Flight Interface</title>
        <para>
          ATA 31 displays show auto flight system status and modes.
        </para>
        <para>
          PERMITTED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Display of autopilot/autothrottle status
        </para>
        <para>
          - Flight director symbology
        </para>
        <para>
          - Mode annunciations on PFD/ND
        </para>
        <para>
          PROHIBITED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Autopilot servo maintenance
        </para>
        <para>
          - Auto flight computer troubleshooting
        </para>
        <para>
          - Flight control system procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          REFERENCE FORMAT: Use "Refer to AMM 22-xx-xx" for auto flight procedures
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>ATA 46 - Information Systems Interface</title>
        <para>
          ATA 31 may interface with cabin information and entertainment systems.
        </para>
        <para>
          PERMITTED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Cockpit-to-cabin data interface specifications
        </para>
        <para>
          - Display of cabin system status in cockpit
        </para>
        <para>
          PROHIBITED in ATA 31:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Cabin management system maintenance
        </para>
        <para>
          - Passenger entertainment system procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          REFERENCE FORMAT: Use "Refer to AMM 46-xx-xx" for cabin systems
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>General Cross-Reference Rules</title>
        <para>
          Rule 1: Reference, Don't Duplicate
        </para>
        <para>
          Always reference other ATA chapters for their content. Never duplicate 
          procedures or descriptions owned by another ATA chapter.
        </para>
        <para>
          Rule 2: Use Proper Reference Format
        </para>
        <para>
          Use &lt;dmRef&gt; elements with proper DMC codes when referencing other 
          ATA chapters. Include sufficient context for the reader to understand 
          why the reference is relevant.
        </para>
        <para>
          Rule 3: Maintain Interface Documentation
        </para>
        <para>
          Document all electrical, data, and physical interfaces to other systems, 
          but limit the description to the interface point, not the connected system.
        </para>
        <para>
          Rule 4: Respect System Boundaries
        </para>
        <para>
          Do not include troubleshooting or maintenance for systems outside ATA 31 
          responsibility, even if they affect indicating/recording functionality.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Interface Control Documents</title>
        <para>
          For complex interfaces, maintain separate Interface Control Documents (ICD):
        </para>
        <para>
          - ATA 31 &lt;-&gt; ATA 24: Power interface ICD
        </para>
        <para>
          - ATA 31 &lt;-&gt; ATA 42: Data bus interface ICD
        </para>
        <para>
          - ATA 31 &lt;-&gt; ATA 45: Maintenance data interface ICD
        </para>
        <para>
          These ICDs should be stored in the 31-00-40-interfaces directory.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
